	--Problem 4. How to copy a log into a folder, zip a folder and submit it on webcourses for dummies. To begin we will first copy the log, first you finish your log! saving it and ensuring it is saved as a .log file(not .txt or anything else). then you will right click on the saved log file and duplicate it. Once duplicated you will move the now copied log file into whichever homework folder required(in this case specifically it was hw1_asalcedo), DONT FORGET to rename your log according to proper naming conventions as given by the class(please see last log entry for directions to the naming convention instructions). Congratulations step 1 is complete and you have now copied your log file into your homework folder, moving on to step 2: how to zip the hw folder. Incredibly similar to the previous step you are first going to navigate to the hw1_username folder(not inside but to the foyer itself), then right click once again and there should be an option to compress the folder, this will turn it into a zip file, and double congratulations you now have your zip file for submission. Finally for the last step all that's left to do is log onto your webcourses and navigate to your specific assignment(in this case for me it was hw1) and upload the indicated zip file then press submit assignment. May these instructions be helpful to those who have forgotten and godspeed :).
